</figure>
            
</div>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{reward}_{\text{format}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>reward</mi><mtext>format</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{reward}_{\text{format}}</annotation></semantics></math> component evaluates the model’s adherence to the expected structured output format, specifically the correct use of XML tags. It is defined as:</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{reward}_{\text{format}}=1.0-\sum_{v\in\mathcal{V}}\text{penalty}(v)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>reward</mi><mtext>format</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext>penalty</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{reward}_{\text{format}}=1.0-\sum_{v\in\mathcal{V}}\text{penalty}(v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of format violations identified in the model’s response. The penalty function <math id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{penalty}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>penalty</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{penalty}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> assigns a predefined cost to each violation, as specified in Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Training Process. ‣ 2.3 ICRL ‣ 2 In-Context Reinforcement Learning (ICRL) ‣ In-Context Reinforcement Learning for Tool Use in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With the proposed reward design, we optimize the policy using the RL objective defined in Equation <a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ GRPO with Tool Use. ‣ 2.2 RL with Tool Use ‣ 2 In-Context Reinforcement Learning (ICRL) ‣ In-Context Reinforcement Learning for Tool Use in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The complete training procedure for <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICRL</span> is outlined in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Reward Design. ‣ 2.3 ICRL ‣ 2 In-Context Reinforcement Learning (ICRL) ‣ In-Context Reinforcement Learning for Tool Use in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S2.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Main Results of <span id="S2.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICRL</span>: Exact Match (EM) Accuracy (%) on various difficult QA datasets. The best performance is set <span id="S2.T3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>. The second best performance is <span id="S2.T3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>.</span></figcaption>
